<article class="env-lemma" id="07BS">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07BS">Lemma <span data-tag="07BS">10.134.11</span>.</a> Let $S \subset A$ is a multiplicative subset of $A$. Let $S^{-1}A \to B$ be a ring map. Then $\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{B/A} \to \mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{B/S^{-1}A}$ is a homotopy equivalence. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Choose a presentation $\alpha : P \to B$ of $B$ over $A$. Then $\beta : S^{-1}P \to B$ is a presentation of $B$ over $S^{-1}A$. A direct computation shows that we have $\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits (\alpha ) = \mathop{N\! L}\nolimits (\beta )$ which proves the lemma as the naive cotangent complex is well defined up to homotopy by Lemma <a href="/tag/00S1" data-tag="00S1">10.134.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>